        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(daemon): self-heal JSON-quoted values in generated service env files (#103804)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #103804.\n\nThe generated gateway service env file could carry entries like `export AWS_REGION='\"us-east-1\"'` — the value itself wrapped in JSON double quotes inside the correct shell single quotes. Sourcing that file makes the env var the literal string `\"us-east-1\"`, which the AWS SDK rejects when building the Bedrock endpoint (`Region not accepted: region=\"\"us-east-1\"\" is not a valid hostname component`).\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe writer (`shellSingleQuote`, `src/daemon/launchd.ts`) and every value-loading path (dotenv parsers, SecretRef resolution, auth-profile/config collectors) pass plain strings — none introduces the quotes. What makes the corruption **permanent** is the round-trip reader: `parseGeneratedEnvValue` (`src/daemon/launchd-plist.ts`) strips only the outer shell single quotes when re-reading the previously generated file on re-stage, preserving the inner JSON pair verbatim. The existing-file preservation feed (`collectPreservedExistingServiceEnvVars` / managed-key re-add in `service-env-render-policy.ts`) then copies the still-quoted value into the new plan and the writer re-wraps it — so every `openclaw doctor --fix` regenerates the same broken value and it never self-heals (exactly the reporter's experience: manual edits persist only until the next regeneration).\n\n### Change\n\n`parseGeneratedEnvValue` now strips one redundant enclosing double-quote pair after shell unquoting. The next re-stage converges: `'\"us-east-1\"'` → `us-east-1` → re-emitted as `'us-east-1'`. Values with interior quotes (`'has \"quotes\" inside'`) are untouched — only a full wrapping pair is treated as corruption.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New regression `src/daemon/launchd-plist.env-values.test.ts` (confirmed failing without the fix): a real temp plist + generated env file with the corrupted `AWS_REGION` entry heals to `us-east-1`, while a plain value and an interior-quotes value round-trip unchanged.\n- `pnpm test src/daemon` — 2 shards passed.\n- `pnpm tsgo:core`, `pnpm tsgo:core:test`, oxfmt, oxlint — clean.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: JSON-quoted values in `~/.openclaw/service-env/<label>.env` break AWS region/credentials and survive every `doctor --fix` regeneration.\nReal environment tested: the real `readLaunchAgentProgramArgumentsFromFile` reader against a real on-disk plist + generated env file reproducing the issue's exact corrupted entry.\nExact steps or command run after this patch: `pnpm test src/daemon/launchd-plist.env-values.test.ts` and `pnpm test src/daemon`.\nEvidence after fix: without the patch the new test fails (`AWS_REGION` reads back as `\"us-east-1\"` with embedded quotes); with it, the value heals to `us-east-1` and non-corrupted values are byte-identical.\nObserved result after fix: the re-stage pipeline converges to clean values; manual file edits are no longer required.\nWhat was not tested: a live launchd install/uninstall cycle on a corrupted host; the healed value flows through the same preservation feed the live doctor --fix path uses. How the JSON pair first entered the environment on the reporter's host remains external to this repo (the value arrived already-quoted); this fix guarantees OpenClaw converges instead of locking it in.\n",
        "branch": "fix/103804-service-env-json-quotes",
